  "step_2": "The individual considers both the difference in the prize amount (100 Euros more in Lottery B) and the difference in winning probabilities (1% lower chance in Lottery B). The individual explicitly notes that Lottery B has a 1% lower chance of winning but offers 100 Euros more. The justification centers on trading off the 1% lower probability for a higher monetary gain. The individual finds it more reasonable to give up 1% probability in favor of the additional 100 Euros. This indicates that the person is weighing the higher outcome against a slightly lower probability, suggesting that the outcome difference is not considered negligible by the individual.",
